#
# INT unit (#107): a struct is a value - every copy (assignment,
# argument, return, foreach variable, capture, element or field read) is
# independent, and a store through a location writes the struct there.
# The functional program runs as a coverage unit too, under the engines
# above, with no second copy (INT-SOURCE); it asserts its own results and
# every engine must print the same.
